From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:17:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: release the ucode resource of a BSS that never started

A BSS can get its ucode resource before it starts, for example while
its interface waits for a CAC or an ACS scan. A BSS that is freed
before it starts must release that resource. Otherwise the registry
keeps a slot that points to freed memory, and the script gets no
remove event.

The teardown of BSS data releases the ucode resource before the
started check, because every teardown path runs that code. The call
does nothing for a BSS without a resource, so the delete of a BSS does
not release the resource itself.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c |    2 +-
 src/ap/ucode.c   |    3 +--
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -848,6 +848,7 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 	hapd->p2p_probe_resp_ie = NULL;
 #endif /* CONFIG_P2P */
 
+	hostapd_ucode_free_bss(hapd);
 	if (!hapd->started) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "%s: Interface %s wasn't started",
 			   __func__, hapd->conf ? hapd->conf->iface : "N/A");
@@ -861,7 +862,6 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 #endif /* CONFIG_OWE */
 
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s(%s)", __func__, hapd->conf->iface);
-	hostapd_ucode_free_bss(hapd);
 	hostapd_ubus_free_bss(hapd);
 	accounting_deinit(hapd);
 	hostapd_deinit_wpa(hapd);
--- a/src/ap/ucode.c
+++ b/src/ap/ucode.c
@@ -478,8 +478,7 @@ uc_hostapd_bss_delete(uc_vm_t *vm, size_
 	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap && hapd->mld)
 		hostapd_mld_beacons_update(hapd);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
-	/* deinit skips these for a bss that never started; both are idempotent */
-	hostapd_ucode_free_bss(hapd);
+	/* deinit skips the ubus release for a bss that never started */
 	hostapd_ubus_free_bss(hapd);
 	hostapd_remove_iface_bss_conf(iface->conf, hapd->conf);
 	hostapd_config_free_bss(hapd->conf);
